ects of personal information in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general aspects of personal information in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies general aspects of personal information in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies general aspects of personal information in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies general aspects of personal information in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Past Time Expressions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about things that happened before. </br> Many sentences that talk about things that happened in the past use a past time expression to show this.<br>Here is a list of past time expressions."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"last (night / week / year \u2026 )\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"when I was \u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yesterday (morning / afternoon) \u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"this (morning / afternoon \u2026 )\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"when you were \u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the day before yesterday \u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"one year ago \u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in 1990 \u2026\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"on Sunday \u2026\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <br> Yesterday I had my Spanish class.<br>This morning I called the college. <br>The day before yesterday I worked at home.<br>On Sunday I hung out with some friends."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use Wh/Hw questions to request information about past events. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <br>When did you go to the park? <br> What time was your appointment? <br> How did you injure your leg?<br> Why did she not come to the party?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the negative form of the past to answer questions. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <br />I didn't go to the park last night. <br />I didn't have an appointment yesterday. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "College Life"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Here are some words and expressions about college.<br><br>You need <span class=\"strong\">to apply </span> and <span class=\"strong\">to be accepted</span> before you can go to a college.<br><br>To apply to a college, you submit an <span class=\"strong\">application</span>.<br><br>A <span class=\"strong\">deadline</span> is the date you need to do something before, like submit your application.<br><br><span class=\"strong\">Credits</span> are points that a student obtains after they finish a course. In North America, students usually get 3 - 6 credits for a course.<br>  <br><span class=\"strong\">Grades</span> are the evaluation of a student's performance in a course. Grades are often letters with symbols + or - (A+, B-, etc.).<br>  <br>A <span class=\"strong\">GPA</span> (Grade Point Average) is the summary of a student's grades in all courses. In North America, a GPA is measured by a number out of 4. A GPA of 3.2 is very good.<br>  "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "credit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "points a student gets after finishing a course"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can take a year off without losing any credits."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use in college."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "GPA"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Grade Point Average -- the average of a student's grades over a period of time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can apply to the program if I have a good GPA."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hung out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "past tense of the verb to hang out"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: On Sunday I hung out with some friends."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to apply"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to ask for permission; like to enter a program or school "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to apply to this college. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to submit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give something formally"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When is the deadline to submit my application? "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le07ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le07ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Do an internet search for colleges in different countries. Use the keyword \u201ccollege\u201d."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find 3 colleges in 3 different English-speaking countries."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out what city each college is located in."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out what students learn there. Is it a high school? A university? A training center?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 2-3 sentences about each college."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the information with your class."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research 3 colleges in 3 different countries."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I prepare a presentation on 3 colleges."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give a presentation."}]}], "type": "sena"}